WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:03.420
- [Mark] Okay, Melvina.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.560
Melvina, where'd you grow up?

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.940
Where are you from originally?

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.120
- I'm originally from
Sanostee, New Mexico.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.160
That's on my mom's side, Dala Silversmith.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.720
But we reside in Oak Springs,

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.463
and that's on my dad's
side, Melvin Silversmith.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.117
- [Mark] And you're Navajo?

00:00:20.117 --> 00:00:21.833
- I'm a full-blooded Navajo.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:28.333
My plans are the (speaking Navajo)

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:36.723
Those are my plans.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:39.503
I'm a proud mother of two.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.400
I have 10 siblings.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:49.680
Nine actually, four
brothers, two passed on.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.630
God bless their soul.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:54.424
I'm 6th. It's five
sisters, six with me, so.

00:00:54.424 --> 00:00:59.413
I'm the baby of the
family. I'm the youngest.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.183
I was taught a lot by my parents.

00:01:05.142 --> 00:01:07.990
I have two different
personalities from both parents

00:01:09.023 --> 00:01:11.980
but combining both personalities

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:15.403
that are coming out through
having a big heart yourself.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.517
- [Mark] How was your childhood?

00:01:19.517 --> 00:01:22.090
- My childhood was pretty good.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:25.113
I was being well taken care
of, but I always got picked on.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:28.920
I always wanted to go
with my parents somewhere,

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.860
but they always chose
my brother before me,

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.223
Merwin Silversmith.

00:01:35.417 --> 00:01:38.100
- [Mark] And did you finish high school?

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:41.123
- I didn't finish high school,
but I did go to Crownpoint.

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:43.423
I went for my GED,

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.263
and I took nursing class on the side.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.140
I pretty much know a lot.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:51.883
I know carpentry, mechanic.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.823
I can build you a house if
you wanna shack out here,

00:01:56.679 --> 00:01:58.029
for those, like us natives.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:00.433
I'll use a cardboard box.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:07.160
But my two kids are safe.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:11.753
They're staying with my ex
sister-in-law, Winifred Watson.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.770
- [Mark] So you don't raise your kids?

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:17.833
- No, I gave her custody.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:20.640
I miss my kids so much,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.060
but with this virus going on,

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:25.240
I ain't trying to harm my kids

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:28.890
or my ex in-laws in any way for that.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.644
- [Mark] So you're living on the street?

00:02:30.644 --> 00:02:31.493
- Living on the streets.

00:02:31.493 --> 00:02:32.923
- [Mark] Here in Gallup, New Mexico.

00:02:32.923 --> 00:02:34.990
- Here in Gallup, New Mexico.

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:37.810
- [Mark] And so, are you
using drugs or alcohol?

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:38.643
Alcohol is your thing?

00:02:38.643 --> 00:02:39.997
- Alcohol.

00:02:39.997 --> 00:02:42.380
- [Mark] How long has alcohol
been a part of your life?

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:45.033
- It's been a part of my
life since high school.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:50.240
Actually, I think mid
school at eighth grade.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:53.300
That's when I first got hit
up by broomstick by my mom

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:58.260
because we were brought up well,

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:01.510
but in our lifetime, we messed up.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:05.340
And the reason why I'm out here is

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:09.160
because I wanted to show my people,

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:12.653
I have a home, I have
a land, I have a ride.

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:17.253
I put all that aside
to live like my people,

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:21.060
to show my people I love them.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.860
Every little thing I have,
this is all I got right here.

00:03:26.977 --> 00:03:30.440
- [Mark] What is your drink of choice?

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:31.747
Is it...

00:03:31.747 --> 00:03:32.580
(Melvina clears throat)

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:35.796
- My drink of choice?

00:03:35.796 --> 00:03:37.396
- [Mark] What do you go to most?

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:42.223
- Hello? This is Gallup,
New Mexico, it's importers.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.440
I've got importer from 505 to 928.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.333
Fallen back on 505, so that's my import.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:54.780
And that's the best alcohol
that would cure a hangover.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:55.900
- [Mark] And what is that?

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:56.922
- Importers.

00:03:56.922 --> 00:03:58.872
- [Mark] But, when you
say importers, what do-

00:03:58.872 --> 00:03:59.916
- Importer Vodka.

00:03:59.916 --> 00:04:01.666
- [Mark] Vodka, okay.

00:04:03.028 --> 00:04:04.982
And do you start drinking
typically in the evening?

00:04:04.982 --> 00:04:07.230
- No, I would buy-

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.500
- [Mark] Cause you're not drunk right now.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:11.500
- No, I would buy a half a gallon,

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:15.230
and it would last me for
like two or three days,

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.033
just walking the streets all night.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.523
I hardly get rest,

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.313
but I'm just glad that I
know that nobody's hurt.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:30.343
Sharing just that little
sip, helping someone else.

00:04:31.719 --> 00:04:33.240
That really means a lot,

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.490
and how much they really appreciate it.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:37.160
- [Mark] So you share your vodka?

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.420
- Mm hmm. I'm not stingy.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.620
Every little thing I
have, I'll give it out.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:48.230
Like my last meal, and that's
a meal I just barely got,

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.623
I'll give it to whoever's hungry.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.577
Or I would tell them to share

00:04:52.577 --> 00:04:55.230
or the last drink, a bottle,

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.335
or I'll give out pints.

00:04:57.335 --> 00:05:01.220
The way I make money is...

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.500
I wouldn't say that.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.610
Question mark. Sell things.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:12.550
But I've been finding
stuff on the streets,

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:14.030
brand new stuff.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.633
I don't know if it was stolen,

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:20.543
but instead of selling it back,

00:05:22.076 --> 00:05:23.463
I give it out.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:27.800
Give it to the most person that needs it.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.453
Like the brand new Nike
shoes I gave away yesterday.

00:05:31.487 --> 00:05:36.487
And that Nike shoe was like
over 179 or almost 200.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:45.690
Man, living these streets is not...

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:47.350
But, I can actually say it's fun

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:50.453
how you make ends meet with each day.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.110
How you gonna survive?

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.233
How are you gonna keep yourself warm?

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:57.493
- [Mark] Sometimes people die

00:05:57.493 --> 00:05:59.101
on the streets from the cold, right?

00:05:59.101 --> 00:06:02.633
- Yeah. If you overdo
your drugs and alcohol.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:06.940
Okay, I'm not gonna beat around the bush.

00:06:09.704 --> 00:06:12.320
When I first came out last year

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:16.167
and in July, I think it was.

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:18.340
It was like August,

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.810
but it was sometimes last year,

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:22.663
I spent almost eight months out here.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:29.789
And one guy came up to me, which
I haven't seen to this day.

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:33.973
He gave me a drink of Vodka Importers.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.150
He goes, "I know what you're here for.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:39.050
I know what you're about.

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:40.807
You're one of them good people."

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:44.470
He goes, "Take a shot at this."

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:47.183
So he gave me a bottle, and I took a shot,

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:52.383
and he goes, "I'm gonna give you heads up.

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:57.113
This, don't take it to get drunk.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:01.210
This, think of it right,
and it'll keep you warm."

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.733
And that was during the cold.

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:07.770
And then he bust out a bud,

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:09.563
like one of those drug buds.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:13.407
It was loaded,

00:07:13.407 --> 00:07:16.007
and I didn't know how to
smoke it, and he taught me.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.520
And he goes, "I'm telling you this

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:20.507
because you're here for your people."

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.827
And I said, "I don't do
drugs. I don't smoke weed."

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:26.970
And he goes, "Just take this,

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:29.130
and I'll tell you what it's about."

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:30.650
So I took the first hit

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.670
and not knowing people were following me,

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:35.910
and people that wanted jump me

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:40.713
for helping out the elderlies
and getting their stuff back.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.863
And he told me this will keep you alert.

00:07:44.901 --> 00:07:47.500
This will tell you, "be careful."

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.810
This is gonna give you a heads up

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:51.453
on who's coming from behind you.

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:56.420
Not knowing better and
actually thinking of it,

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:59.670
and then thinking about always how smoke,

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:01.763
we looked through smoke ashes,

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:04.803
and I thought about that.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:07.050
The whole time I was out here,

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:08.733
I took alcohol and drugs,

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:13.060
but I used it in a good way,

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:14.193
not in a bad way.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.550
I help people. I help elderlies.

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:19.853
I help them survive.

00:08:20.891 --> 00:08:23.773
I've seen things that
I should've not seen.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:28.180
I could say I've seen the unexplainable,

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:32.730
the unexpectable, but I
explored that adventure.

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:35.480
- [Mark] What's the most
extreme thing you've seen

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:37.080
in your time here on the street?

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.390
- My most extreme?

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:45.390
I've seen a guy who's the
opposite of a Navajo medicine man.

00:08:50.738 --> 00:08:54.017
I've seen him get lifted
up off the ground frozen.

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.853
And that guy did not like me.

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:02.820
The day I seen him get lifted

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:05.410
and put it into an ambulance all frozen,

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:07.023
I cried, and I prayed.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:10.283
Prayer means a lot.

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:14.260
But by morning,

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:16.937
the next morning, I got up and I was like,

00:09:16.937 --> 00:09:19.487
"Damn, I was worried
about the guy so much."

00:09:21.492 --> 00:09:22.325
Next you know, he was walking right there

00:09:22.325 --> 00:09:24.480
in front of (indistinct)

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:26.460
I just told my uncle to stop.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:27.850
I jumped off.

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:32.040
I ran to him, and I said,
"Dude, can I get a hug?"

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:33.240
And he said, "For what?"

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:36.397
I go, "I've seen you die yesterday."

00:09:39.324 --> 00:09:40.157
And I said,

00:09:41.587 --> 00:09:44.547
"Just right there between
(indistinct) and Third Street."

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:50.117
I said, "The way they lifted
you, you were frozen, Dude."

00:09:51.869 --> 00:09:52.702
And I said, "I'm sorry,

00:09:52.702 --> 00:09:57.702
but it means a lot that
my prayers did go through

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:00.420
because you're still here
walking in the morning."

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:06.103
And stupid me, I had drinks, I had hits,

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:12.290
and I told him, I said, "Hey
guy, I'm not gonna do this.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.947
I hate to do this, but shoot, man,

00:10:15.947 --> 00:10:17.987
it's nice to see you alive."

00:10:19.292 --> 00:10:22.533
I offer him that shot, offer him hits,

00:10:23.429 --> 00:10:25.953
and then he said he was
brought back to life.

00:10:28.269 --> 00:10:32.940
I've seen an older lady get
jumped by three teenagers.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:37.567
Shoot, I go back, and I told them,

00:10:37.567 --> 00:10:41.080
"What if that was your mom,
your sister, or your grandma?

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:42.593
Would you like it? Seeing it?

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:46.538
You give her stuff back. She don't drink.

00:10:46.538 --> 00:10:50.630
She don't do drugs.
Can't you guys see that?"

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:54.403
And they gave her a cut
on her left eyebrow.

00:10:58.530 --> 00:10:59.840
- [Melvina] People think it's funny.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:01.323
They think life is funny.

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:05.430
They make fun of life.

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:08.600
That's why they're where
they're at right now,

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.233
stealing from other people.

00:11:12.723 --> 00:11:14.570
If you help somebody out,

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:18.240
shoot, God has something
in return ahead of you.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:19.550
I find free things.

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:22.720
I find brand new shoes.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:24.670
And it's only telling me to pass it on.

00:11:25.550 --> 00:11:29.527
Somebody claims it's
theirs, and I tell them,

00:11:29.527 --> 00:11:31.770
"Look, I've seen you out here for so long,

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:34.560
and you think it's your
shoe when you stole it?"

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:38.993
Why hang on to something
you stole? Pass it on.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:42.790
Because that person you stole

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:45.420
from is not gonna ever get it back,

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:47.520
but they'll see another person wearing it.

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:52.260
And for people to be discriminating,

00:11:52.260 --> 00:11:53.623
being disrespectful,

00:11:54.843 --> 00:11:57.920
the only way you're gonna live out here,

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:02.750
you're gonna survive is by your own self,

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:06.713
your being honest, you have loyalty,

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:11.243
be independent to live on the streets.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:14.853
You help one, you shall receive help.

00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:17.963
Either way, it works.

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:22.363
You disrespect people, you
get that same disrespect.

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:27.083
How are you gonna get respect
when you make fun of a person?

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:31.290
If they're disabled, if they can't walk,

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:32.460
they fall over, shoot,

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:35.130
you go over there and lift their hand.

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:37.480
You don't just watch them
and make fun of them.

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:43.653
Most people out here
think they know better.

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:48.973
All the dealers, they're all gone.

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:52.167
Now, I told them,

00:12:52.167 --> 00:12:54.150
"You guys are disrespecting so much

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:57.129
that it's gonna come back worse on you."

00:12:57.129 --> 00:13:01.153
However is the B-I-T-C-H.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:04.510
- [Mark] Is there a sex work here?

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:07.360
Sex trafficking going on in New Mexico?

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:08.620
- Sex trafficking?

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:10.763
I know like some of the hotels,

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:16.210
they have room for prostitute,

00:13:16.210 --> 00:13:18.193
and it's my own native girls.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.693
But what they get out of it is $5.

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:27.270
They get a drink. They just get one shot.

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:28.363
Some shoot up.

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:34.270
You see them normal, happy,
but once they get on that,

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:35.920
they're a whole different person.

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:37.730
It's like...

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:41.933
How would you call it?

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:47.913
They're making fun of themselves,

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:52.120
but they don't know that drugs,

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:55.103
alcohol is making them look stupid.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:58.759
All these girls here, they're parents,

00:13:58.759 --> 00:14:00.800
not one acts like one.

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:02.030
They act like gangsters.

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:06.473
They act like they can hurt somebody.

00:14:07.770 --> 00:14:10.320
But shoot, once a guy, backhands them,

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.183
they're the ones crying, running.

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:16.140
For me, as a mother of two,

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:18.253
I'm proud to have my beautiful kids.

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:21.373
I'm glad they're safe and alive.

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:26.210
But I ain't out here to beat another guy.

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:27.913
I ain't out here to start trouble.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:32.203
I'm out here to show
love and caring again.

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:36.363
I just tell them, "Hey
man, love you guys."

00:14:36.363 --> 00:14:38.110
- [Mark] So why you on the streets

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:40.217
rather than with your children?

00:14:40.217 --> 00:14:42.273
- My children are safe.

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:46.100
After quarantine, my sister got it twice,

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:48.030
her and her girlfriend,

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:51.630
and I risked my life to
be out here to watch her.

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:53.380
The girlfriend won't take her home.

00:14:55.070 --> 00:14:57.210
She messed up my sister's face so bad

00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:59.293
that her face is barely healing.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:02.290
I tell them. I watch over them.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:05.603
They sleep on top of the
bridge on Third Street.

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:10.880
I'm afraid that the girlfriend

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.430
might push her off that bridge.

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:17.203
And I stay at the bottom looking out,

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:19.860
not just watching my sister,

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:22.090
I'm watching everybody.

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:24.123
Walkway is a dangerous place.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:31.143
I mean, one person, so little,
makes themselves look big.

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:35.397
I say, "Hey, little big men."

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:39.770
I say, "You don't got no balls

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:41.857
to be treating your people like this."

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.870
I got guys sent out to me.

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:46.970
I got a knife pulled out to me last night.

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:50.560
And I took my sister and her girlfriend,

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:52.385
and I said, "You guys, don't be around me,

00:15:52.385 --> 00:15:55.996
but just stay somewhere
where they won't see you."

00:15:55.996 --> 00:15:58.046
And I haven't seen them since last night.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:03.603
- [Mark] Do you relate
to your Navajo heritage?

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:07.453
- My Navajo heritage? Yeah, I do.

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:11.223
I'm a hand trembler in a good way.

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:15.847
I'm here to let people know, "Watch out."

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:21.270
It's not like in no bad way.

00:16:21.270 --> 00:16:22.483
I heal people.

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:26.990
I'm just glad that I have the most

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:30.323
two loving caring parents
who taught us well.

00:16:33.834 --> 00:16:35.150
I don't know if I get it from my mom

00:16:35.150 --> 00:16:40.150
or my dad's side, but the
bond of love, I'm showing it.

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:43.663
I've seen people get off
the street from my words.

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:48.670
I haven't seen them, but I
do see them other places.

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:49.580
They give me a hug,

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:52.883
and they tell me my words
are of encouragement.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.863
I'm an independent person.

00:16:57.955 --> 00:16:59.783
I'm not out here to make fun,

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:02.370
not to act like a fool.

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:04.233
I'm not out here to fight people.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:06.979
But when it comes to a point,

00:17:06.979 --> 00:17:09.183
that point will become a point.

00:17:11.603 --> 00:17:14.280
How else are you gonna survive?

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:17.540
They take stuff from
you, and you see someone.

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:19.190
They're trying to make you fight.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:23.920
My own people would be like that.

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:25.193
And that's not right.

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:28.723
I'm out here to show love, caring,

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:32.373
how it feels to have love again.

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:37.173
Ain't nobody showing it.

00:17:38.940 --> 00:17:41.573
I gave up everything,
and this is all I got.

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:46.220
I'm ashamed to ask for money.

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:50.447
I'm ashamed to be like,
"Can I borrow some change?"

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:55.830
But damn, I'm glad I'm still alive,

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:58.250
and I still see my
people alive the next day

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:00.373
with a smile.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:04.823
People discriminate us, other racists,

00:18:06.027 --> 00:18:10.890
when my people panhandle,
telling them to get a job.

00:18:10.890 --> 00:18:12.960
They don't know what we're going through.

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:15.233
We are the first ones that suffered.

00:18:17.600 --> 00:18:22.060
We are the ones that went
into our world to survive.

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:25.350
We went through the long walk, shoot.

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:28.163
You might even be Navajo
too. You don't know it.

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:31.723
You have a color of Navajo on you.

00:18:32.661 --> 00:18:34.111
(indistinct) what's up Ninja?

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:37.973
But I always show love to everybody.

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:41.400
I try to keep a drink on me

00:18:42.530 --> 00:18:46.433
because anxiety is not a funny thing.

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:51.853
You see people get DTs,
anxiety, falling over.

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:55.313
People just make fun and walk off.

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:58.853
The guy's suffering. The lady's suffering.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.103
Who does that?

00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:06.383
I would do anything to
lend a hand, lend a finger.

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:10.967
Most people say, "I got your back."

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:13.210
How are they gonna get your back

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.770
when they just run off
when you get into trouble?

00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:17.840
When someone steps up to you,

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.263
I tell my people, I got your front.

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:25.223
I'll take a hit for
you, but I'll dodge it.

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:31.136
So you don't know if I'll throw fake left,

00:19:31.136 --> 00:19:33.543
but I'll knock you out with the right.

00:19:34.550 --> 00:19:37.350
I'll straight out kick you
in your face without knowing.

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:41.130
- [Melvina] I'm not here to fight.

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:44.333
I'm here to love and care for people.

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:50.423
And to see them not around,
shoot, I save lives.

00:19:52.702 --> 00:19:53.845
- [Mark] All right, Melvina.

00:19:53.845 --> 00:19:55.603
Well, thank you so much
for talking with me.

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:57.830
- But you might be my native,

00:19:57.830 --> 00:20:02.003
so I'm glad I did this.

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:05.633
But my natives, I love them.

00:20:05.633 --> 00:20:06.466
(Mark chuckles)

00:20:06.466 --> 00:20:07.703
But they're my ninjas.

00:20:08.577 --> 00:20:10.968
- [Mark] All right,
Melvina, thank you so much.

00:20:10.968 --> 00:20:12.203
- Thank you so much.

00:20:12.203 --> 00:20:14.603
And just, love you, mom and dad.

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:20.659
Love you Delilah, Jana
Watson, my beautiful kids.

00:20:20.659 --> 00:20:23.326
(lips smacking)

